  "name": "z0r0z V4 Router hardcoded calldata-offset payer check bypass",
  "summary": "UniswapV4Router04.swap(bytes,uint256) checked the payer by comparing calldataload(164) with caller(), assuming the data argument sits at offset 0x40. Attackers moved the bytes offset, planted their own address at byte 164 and named a victim with a standing router approval as BaseData.payer, so the router pulled the victim's tokens and paid the swap output to them.",
